---
description: How and when to subscribe to real-time channels.
alwaysApply: false
---

When fetching a list of items, it is sometimes useful to subscribe to a real-time channel. To do so, you can use the helper function in `utils/SupabaseUtils.ts`. Never set two subscription to same table, it won't work (it will cancel the first subscription) use filters wisely.

import { createRealTimeUpdates } from "@/utils/SupabaseUtils";
import { useAuth } from "@/contexts/AuthContext";
import { updateOrInsertInListWithId } from "@/utils/Utils";
import { useWorkspace } from "@/contexts/WorkspaceContext";

const { selectedWorkspace } = useWorkspace();
const channelRef = useRef<any>(null);
const [itemList, setItemList] = useState([]);

useEffect(() => {
        setItemList(fetchInitialList());
        ...
        let currentChannel: any;

        createRealTimeUpdates(
            {
                table: "itemTable",
                onFileChange: (newRecord) => {
                        if (newRecord.workspace_id !== selectedWorkspace.id) return;
                        setItemList((prev) => updateOrInsertInListWithId(prev, newRecord));
                        },
                 channelRef,
                 onSuccess: (channel) => {
                    currentChannel = channel; // ✅ Store the channel instance when successfully subscribed
                },
                selectedWorkspaceId: selectedWorkspace.id
            }
        );
        return () => {
            if (currentChannel) {
                currentChannel.unsubscribe();
            }
        };
    }, [selectedWorkspace?.id, userProfile?.id]);


Here, we filter the real-time channel by workspace ID and double-check in `onFileChange`. You could also check another condition such as `created_by`. However, during subscription, only one filter is allowed (despite poor Supabase documentation at the time of writing, 30/09/2025). If you want another filter, you can set
`customFilter = \`created_by=eq.${userProfile.id}\`` for example. This overwrites the workspace ID filter. Only one filter is allowed.


Note: `onFileChange` can, of course, perform whatever is needed. The helper function `updateOrInsertInListWithId` will:

 - Remove the item from the list if `deleted_dt` is not null
 - Insert if it does not exist in the list, or update it
 - Reorder by `created_at` (or another key) if needed
 
See the definition in `utils/Utils.ts`.


If it is not working, suggest that the user double-check that “Enable Realtime” is ON in Supabase.

In rare cases, if the row is too large, it might be useful to run:

ALTER TABLE my_table REPLICA IDENTITY FULL;

to ensure that the full row is retrieved, not just the primary keys.

